(Bug #40's other half: rejecting a scalar operand must not cost `Write` the
 operands it has always taken. A text writes its characters, a buffer writes
 its bytes, and a format string renders the very scalars that are refused
 bare - which is the fix the diagnostic names, so this test is what that
 message promises. The last pair is the value diagnostic's promise: a value
 is refused, but copied into a typed variable it writes, whatever it holds.)

a number called temperature is 72.
a float called humidity is 36.5.
a boolean called ready is true.
a text called label is "sensor".

Create a buffer called units.
append " C" to units.

a value called anything is "dynamic".
a text called settled is anything.

a text called path is "/tmp/vox_bug40_write.txt".
open a file for writing called report at path.
Write label to report.
Write " " to report.
Write "{temperature} {humidity} {ready}" to report.
Write units to report.
Write " " to report.
Write settled to report.
close report.

Create a buffer called readback.
open a file for reading called saved at path.
read from saved into readback.
close saved.
Print readback.
Delete the file path.
